WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.822
Theo’s license is good for two years, expiring

00:00:02.822 --> 00:00:05.291
at the end of his birth month.

00:00:05.291 --> 00:00:08.818
Renewal needs the renewal application, the fees and continued qualification.

00:00:08.818 --> 00:00:11.992
Continuing education runs on an earlier clock: the hours

00:00:11.992 --> 00:00:14.814
must be finished before the renewal is filed.

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:18.341
The Administration sends renewal notices to the address and email

00:00:18.341 --> 00:00:21.868
on file, so a producer who moved and never updated

00:00:21.868 --> 00:00:25.043
his record may miss the notice and the deadline.

00:00:25.043 --> 00:00:28.923
Theo marks two dates on his calendar, the education deadline and

00:00:28.923 --> 00:00:32.450
the expiration, and treats the first as the real one.

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:37.117
A regular Maryland resident producer must complete 24 hours of approved continuing

00:00:37.117 --> 00:00:41.784
education in each two-year renewal period, including at least three hours in

00:00:41.784 --> 00:00:46.062
ethics, with the hours satisfying the requirements of the lines held.

00:00:46.062 --> 00:00:49.562
The statute requires the education to be completed no

00:00:49.562 --> 00:00:52.673
later than 15 days before the license expires.

00:00:52.673 --> 00:00:57.340
An older Administration chart still says 30 days; the current statute controls.

00:00:57.340 --> 00:01:01.229
Special provisions reduce the hours for producers with long service

00:01:01.229 --> 00:01:05.119
who file the required affidavit, limited lines have exceptions, and

00:01:05.119 --> 00:01:09.008
a nonresident satisfies Maryland through compliance in the home state.

00:01:09.008 --> 00:01:11.730
This course is not approved continuing education.

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:14.677
An expired license is not a grace period.

00:01:14.677 --> 00:01:18.729
Theo may not sell, solicit or negotiate until reinstatement takes effect.

00:01:18.729 --> 00:01:22.780
For up to one year after expiration he may reinstate by

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:26.832
filing the application, paying the renewal fee, the fraud prevention fee

00:01:26.832 --> 00:01:30.884
and a 100 dollar reinstatement fee, and proving the required education.

00:01:30.884 --> 00:01:34.936
If he applies within 60 days of expiration, the reinstatement is

00:01:34.936 --> 00:01:38.988
retroactive to the expiration date; after 60 days it is prospective

00:01:38.988 --> 00:01:42.671
only, leaving a gap during which any sales were unlicensed.

00:01:42.671 --> 00:01:46.355
After one year the license is gone and he must

00:01:46.355 --> 00:01:49.670
apply as a new applicant and retake the exam.

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:53.682
A licensee must report a change of legal name, trade name,

00:01:53.682 --> 00:01:57.329
email address or home or business address within 30 days.

00:01:57.329 --> 00:02:00.247
A business entity has a separate ten-day rule

00:02:00.247 --> 00:02:03.165
for changes to its designated producer’s required information.

00:02:03.165 --> 00:02:08.272
A producer who changes legal residence to another state has a 30-day certification duty,

00:02:08.272 --> 00:02:13.378
and a producer moving into Maryland must apply for resident authority within 90 days.

00:02:13.378 --> 00:02:17.025
Trade names are filed with the Administration before use; adopting

00:02:17.025 --> 00:02:20.673
an assumed name on a website does not file it.

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:24.320
Updating the agency’s letterhead changes nothing in the licensing record.

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:26.186
Two reports protect the public.

00:02:26.186 --> 00:02:31.412
If a producer is prosecuted for a crime, other than a vehicle-related misdemeanor, he

00:02:31.412 --> 00:02:36.638
must report it to the Commissioner within 30 days of the initial appearance in

00:02:36.638 --> 00:02:41.490
court, with the charging document, any court order and other relevant legal documents.

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:44.103
Waiting for a conviction is too late.

00:02:44.103 --> 00:02:47.836
If another state or jurisdiction takes an administrative action against

00:02:47.836 --> 00:02:51.569
his license, he must report that within 30 days of

00:02:51.569 --> 00:02:54.928
the final disposition, with the order or consent order.

00:02:54.928 --> 00:02:58.661
Theo’s AMG manager cannot report for him; the duty is

00:02:58.661 --> 00:03:02.020
personal, and failing it is itself grounds for discipline.

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:03.139
Picture Theo’s year.

00:03:03.139 --> 00:03:07.242
In March he moves and updates his address within 30 days.

00:03:07.242 --> 00:03:12.465
In June he finishes his 24 hours, including ethics, well before the 15-day deadline.

00:03:12.465 --> 00:03:16.568
In August he files the renewal before his birth month ends.

00:03:16.568 --> 00:03:21.417
In October he is charged with a misdemeanor unrelated to driving and reports

00:03:21.417 --> 00:03:26.266
it within 30 days of his first court date, attaching the charging document.

00:03:26.266 --> 00:03:29.997
Each event has its own clock and its own trigger.

00:03:29.997 --> 00:03:34.100
A producer who keeps these dates keeps the license; a producer

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:37.830
who assumes the agency will handle them risks losing it.
